Emerging Market Opportunities
Expansion of Advanced Packaging Applications
The growth of chiplet architectures, fan-out wafer-level packaging, and heterogeneous integration is creating demand for coating technologies suited to complex surface profiles. Spray coaters can support the deposition of protective and functional materials across non-planar structures.

Development of Compound Semiconductor Manufacturing
Growing adoption of silicon carbide (SiC), gallium nitride (GaN), and other compound semiconductor materials in electric vehicles, renewable energy, and telecommunications is creating opportunities for specialized wafer-processing equipment.

Automation and Smart Process Monitoring
Integration of machine vision, automated nozzle control, and real-time process monitoring can improve coating consistency and reduce material waste. Equipment suppliers that incorporate advanced process analytics may gain an advantage in high-volume semiconductor manufacturing.

